    "brief": "Surface created from curves",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Surface creation workflows can benefit from domain remapping techniques. The flatten-bounds approach for global domain normalization (flattening data tree before Bounds component) ensures consistent UV coordinate systems across multiple curves. Consider UV parameterization when creating surfaces from point sequences.\n\nRelated insight: Recipe S18E04 demonstrates a 20-component workflow example, showing mid-complexity implementations between simple approaches and 75+ component systems.\n\nRelated insight: S19 series complexity progression: S19E01 (30) → S19E03 (44) → S19E02 (45), showing gradual complexity scaling in parametric surface workflows.",
